---
/**
 * Supporting Editorial Content for Image Resizer
 *
 * Explains bicubic pixel interpolation, aspect-ratio preservation,
 * percentage vs dimension workflows, format choices, and verified privacy guarantees.
 */
---

<article class="prose prose-slate max-w-none space-y-12 mb-14">
  <!-- 1. How does image resizing work? -->
  <section aria-labelledby="how-resizing-works-heading">
    <div class="rounded-2xl bg-white border border-surface-200/80 p-6 sm:p-8 shadow-xs">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2.5 mb-4">
        <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-brand-100 text-brand-700 flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-sm" aria-hidden="true">
          i
        </div>
        <h2 id="how-resizing-works-heading" class="text-xl font-bold text-surface-900">
          How does image resizing work?
        </h2>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-3.5 text-xs sm:text-sm text-surface-600 leading-relaxed max-w-none">
        <p>
          Every digital photograph consists of a fixed grid of color pixels. <strong>Image resizing</strong> modifies the total width and height of this grid to match specific display dimensions, email limits, or website requirements.
        </p>
        <p>
          Our in-browser resizer uses HTML5 Canvas with high-quality <strong>bicubic interpolation</strong> (<code class="text-brand-700 bg-brand-50 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">imageSmoothingQuality = 'high'</code>). When downscaling, the algorithm calculates a weighted mathematical average of surrounding pixel clusters to produce sharp, crisp results without jagged staircase edges or moiré patterns.
        </p>
        <p>
          Keeping the <strong>aspect ratio locked</strong> ensures that horizontal and vertical proportions scale symmetrically. For example, reducing a 1200 × 800 photo to 600 pixels wide automatically sets the height to 400 pixels, preventing unnatural stretching or squishing.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 2. Resize by pixels or percentage -->
  <section aria-labelledby="pixels-vs-percentage-heading">
    <div class="rounded-2xl bg-white border border-surface-200/80 p-6 sm:p-8 shadow-xs">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2.5 mb-3">
        <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-indigo-100 text-indigo-700 flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-sm" aria-hidden="true">
          ⇄
        </div>
        <div>
          <h2 id="pixels-vs-percentage-heading" class="text-xl font-bold text-surface-900">
            Resize by pixels or percentage
          </h2>
          <p class="text-xs text-surface-500 mt-0.5">Choosing the right sizing method for your workflow</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mt-6 not-prose">
        <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-surface-50 border border-surface-200 space-y-2">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="px-2 py-0.5 rounded bg-brand-100 text-brand-800 font-bold text-xs uppercase tracking-wider">By Dimensions (Pixels)</span>
          </div>
          <p class="text-xs text-surface-600 leading-relaxed">
            Ideal when you must satisfy strict platform specifications. Examples include social media cover banners (e.g. 1200 × 630 px), marketplace product thumbnails (e.g. 800 × 800 px), or passport upload forms requiring exact pixel bounds.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-surface-50 border border-surface-200 space-y-2">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="px-2 py-0.5 rounded bg-brand-100 text-brand-800 font-bold text-xs uppercase tracking-wider">By Percentage (%)</span>
          </div>
          <p class="text-xs text-surface-600 leading-relaxed">
            Best for batches containing mixed orientations and varying dimensions. Setting a scale factor like <strong>50%</strong> shrinks each photo to half its original width and height, preserving unique aspect ratios across every image in the batch.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 3. Image formats and quality -->
  <section aria-labelledby="formats-and-quality-heading">
    <div class="rounded-2xl bg-white border border-surface-200/80 p-6 sm:p-8 shadow-xs">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2.5 mb-4">
        <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-emerald-100 text-emerald-700 flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-sm" aria-hidden="true">
          ✦
        </div>
        <h2 id="formats-and-quality-heading" class="text-xl font-bold text-surface-900">
          Image formats and quality
        </h2>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-3.5 text-xs sm:text-sm text-surface-600 leading-relaxed max-w-none">
        <p>
          You can output resized images in their original format or convert between standard web formats:
        </p>
        <ul class="space-y-2 list-disc list-inside">
          <li><strong>JPG / JPEG:</strong> The universal format for camera photographs. Adjust the quality slider (50% to 100%) to balance file weight against detail. Note: Because JPEG lacks an alpha channel, transparent PNG or WebP images are composited over a clean white background.</li>
          <li><strong>PNG:</strong> Lossless format ideal for logos, screenshots, diagrams, and illustrations requiring transparent backgrounds. PNG compression is lossless, so the lossy quality slider is automatically disabled.</li>
          <li><strong>WebP:</strong> Modern web standard developed by Google that delivers superior compression compared to JPG at equivalent visual quality while supporting full alpha transparency.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 4. Client-Side Privacy Guarantee -->
  <section aria-labelledby="privacy-guarantee-heading">
    <div class="rounded-2xl bg-white border border-surface-200/80 p-6 sm:p-8 shadow-xs">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2.5 mb-3">
        <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-lg bg-emerald-100 text-emerald-700 flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-sm" aria-hidden="true">
          ✓
        </div>
        <div>
          <h2 id="privacy-guarantee-heading" class="text-xl font-bold text-surface-900">
            Client-Side Privacy Guarantee
          </h2>
          <p class="text-xs text-surface-500 mt-0.5">Your personal photos, scans, and graphic designs never leave your device</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="text-surface-600 leading-relaxed mt-3 text-xs sm:text-sm">
        Many online image resizers upload your photos to third-party cloud servers where they may be logged, analyzed, or stored. Our resizer executes <strong>100% in your browser's local memory</strong>:
      </p>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-4 mt-6 text-xs not-prose">
        <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-surface-50 border border-surface-200">
          <strong class="text-surface-900 block font-semibold mb-1">Zero Server Uploads</strong>
          <p class="text-surface-600">Pixel data is decoded and scaled directly on your GPU/CPU via HTML5 Canvas. Zero bytes are uploaded.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-surface-50 border border-surface-200">
          <strong class="text-surface-900 block font-semibold mb-1">Confidential Images</strong>
          <p class="text-surface-600">Private contracts, family pictures, and confidential prototypes remain entirely on your device.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-surface-50 border border-surface-200">
          <strong class="text-surface-900 block font-semibold mb-1">Offline Capability</strong>
          <p class="text-surface-600">After page load, the resizer continues to function reliably even without an internet connection.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</article>
